<section id="basics" class="basics" style="background:var(--panel)"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="head">
    <p class="eyebrow">The basics</p>
    <h2>Every cell is listening, and every cell is talking</h2>
    <p>Think of your body as a huge orchestra. Trillions of cells need to play in time, and they do it by sending each other signals. Redox signalling is one of the ways they communicate. It's a normal part of biology, and scientists have studied it for decades.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="cards">
    <div class="card" style="background:var(--bg)">
      <span class="n">1</span>
      <h3>The messengers</h3>
      <p>Your cells make small, reactive molecules as part of everyday life. Researchers now understand that some of them act as messengers, not just as by-products.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="background:var(--bg)">
      <span class="n">2</span>
      <h3>The balance</h3>
      <p>Healthy cells keep these signals in balance. Scientists call this redox balance, and it's an active field of research into how we age and adapt.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="background:var(--bg)">
      <span class="n">3</span>
      <h3>The whole picture</h3>
      <p>Sleep, movement, morning light, good food, stress and connection all shape the environment your cells live in. No single thing is the answer.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="quote">Knowing the science means very little if we don't live it.</p>
</div></section>

<section id="story" class="story"><div class="wrap">
  <figure style="margin:0"><img src="staff.jpg" alt="Sepp in a blue linen shirt holding a carved walking staff" width="872" height="1304" loading="lazy"></figure>
  <div class="txt">
    <p class="eyebrow">Why this matters to me</p>
    <h2>Born in the mid-60s. Now thriving in my 60s.</h2>
    <p>I've spent most of my life building homes and timber structures with my hands, and most of my mornings in the ocean. At 61, I'm still building. These days it's strength, health, relationships and community.</p>
    <p>My mornings start the same way: Kundalini yoga, the sunrise, then the gym or the pool. I see wellbeing as many pieces of one picture, and learning about how the body works at the cellular level is one piece I've found fascinating for over a decade.</p>
    <div class="salt">
      <strong>It starts with salt water</strong>
      The redox supplement I take each day begins as salt and purified water, transformed through a patented process developed by ASEA. For a bloke who's always been drawn to the sea, I love that.
    </div>
    <p>I've been with ASEA for 12 years, and every month I give to Advancing Life, its foundation supporting families and communities around the world.</p>
