<section id="questions" class="questions"><div class="wrap">
  <p class="eyebrow">The honest questions</p>
  <h2>What people usually ask me</h2>
  <p class="intro">Good questions deserve straight answers. If yours isn't here, ask me.</p>
  <div class="faq">
    <details>
      <summary>Isn't this just another antioxidant?</summary>
      <div class="a"><p>No. Antioxidants aim to neutralise reactive molecules. Redox signalling is about the balance and communication between them, which is a different idea. ASEA's own site explains how its products relate to this.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What is ASEA?</summary>
      <div class="a"><p>ASEA is a global company, based in Utah in the USA, that makes redox supplements and skincare. Its products are available in Australia and many other countries through independent brand partners like me.</p><p>For me, it's always been more than that. At an ASEA global event, these words went up on the big screen, and they say it better than I can:</p><blockquote style="margin:4px 0;padding:4px 0 4px 18px;border-left:2px solid var(--sun);font-family:var(--display);font-size:1.2rem;line-height:1.4">This is not a company. This is a global tribe united in purpose, ethos, science and service.</blockquote><p>That's what I've found over 12 years: people in many countries who care about doing life and business well, together.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Is it a medicine? Will it fix my health problem?</summary>
      <div class="a"><p>No. It's a supplement, not a medicine, and I'm not a doctor. If you have a health condition, please talk with your doctor or health professional. What I share here is my own experience and general education.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I have to buy anything?</summary>
      <div class="a"><p>Not at all. I'm happy to just have a conversation. If you'd like to try the products, you can explore and order directly on my ASEA page, in your own time.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Is there a business opportunity?</summary>
      <div class="a"><p>Yes, for those who want it. I've built an ASEA business over 12 years without ever pushing anyone, and I love mentoring people who want to make a difference. If that interests you, let's talk.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Where can I read the research for myself?</summary>
      <div class="a"><p>Redox signalling is one of the most studied areas of cell biology, with thousands of published papers. Two good places to start:</p><p><a href="https://redoxscience.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Redox Science</a> shares plain-language summaries of redox research.<br><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=redox+signaling" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PubMed</a>, the US National Library of Medicine's free database, lets you search the published studies yourself.</p><p>Most of this research looks at redox biology in general rather than at any one product. ASEA also works with scientific partners around the world, including researchers at the University of Southampton and the University of Bath in the UK, the University of California, Berkeley, the University of Valencia in Spain, the University of Chile, and here in Australia, Professor Gerald Münch at Western Sydney University.</p><p>If you'd like to know more about the research on ASEA's own products, ask me and I'll point you to the source.</p></div>
    </details>
  </div>
</div></section>

